  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `record_failure` in `billing/dunning.py`. The existing suite passes (24 tests). I didn't add the reproducing test to the suite, so I haven't run it.\n\nWhen retries ran out on an invoice whose subscription was already canceled (or had none), the code called `mark_uncollectible(ctx, invoice[\"final_action\"])`. `final_action` is a dunning policy field, not an invoice field, so that raised the `KeyError`. It now passes `invoice[\"id\"]`, which is what the `cancel` branch below it already does.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repository root:\n`{\"file\": \"dunning.py\", \"function\": \"record_failure\"}`",
